{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q28209590","formula":"C₁₁H₁₀F₃N₃O₄","hill":"C11H10F3N3O4","elements":["H","C","N","O","F"],"composition":{"C":11.0,"F":3.0,"H":10.0,"N":3.0,"O":4.0},"names":{"en":"RU-22930"},"descriptions":{"en":"RU-22930 is a nonsteroidal antiandrogen (NSAA) related to the NSAAs flutamide and nilutamide (RU-23908) and was developed by Roussel Uclaf but was never marketed. It is a selective antagonist of the androgen receptor and consequently has progonadotropic effects by increasing gonadotropin and testosterone levels via disinhibition of the hypothalamic-pituitary-gonadal axis. Unlike flutamide and nilutamide, the drug is said to be short-acting and inactive by injection, but it has been found to be active topically in animals, and hence could be useful for the treatment of androgen-dependent skin conditions."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":9948430,"mass":305.21,"charge":0,"smiles":"CN1C(=O)N(CCO1)C2=CC(=C(C=C2)[N+](=O)[O-])C(F)(F)F","inchikey":"SQAORNVRAYTOMS-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-methyl-4-[4-nitro-3-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]-1,2,4-oxadiazinan-3-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"9948430","atoms":31,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-3.635,"y":-1.597,"z":0.774,"el":"F"},{"x":-3.537,"y":-1.226,"z":-1.367,"el":"F"},{"x":-2.232,"y":-2.707,"z":-0.453,"el":"F"},{"x":4.586,"y":-1.135,"z":0.03,"el":"O"},{"x":2.811,"y":1.867,"z":-0.688,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.749,"y":2.528,"z":0.353,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.348,"y":0.449,"z":-0.015,"el":"O"},{"x":1.985,"y":-0.166,"z":0.134,"el":"N"},{"x":4.298,"y":0.214,"z":-0.237,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.466,"y":1.321,"z":0.165,"el":"N"},{"x":2.323,"y":-1.545,"z":0.501,"el":"C"},{"x":0.59,"y":0.208,"z":0.14,"el":"C"},{"x":3.725,"y":-1.602,"z":1.054,"el":"C"},{"x":3.011,"y":0.717,"z":-0.285,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.388,"y":-0.763,"z":-0.05